  <h1>Razor clams, persillade <em>and chorizo</em></h1>
  <p class="chapo">The land-and-sea starter that sums up Gabin's cooking: shellfish, garlic and parsley butter, and the gentle heat of grilled chorizo.</p>
</header>

<section class="section" style="padding-top:1rem">
  <div class="conteneur duo">
    <div>
      <h2>Sea and land on the same plate</h2>
      <p>Razor clams (<span lang="fr">couteaux</span>) are long, slender shellfish with fine, slightly sweet flesh. Gabin prepares them with a persillade, the classic French mix of garlic and parsley, and lifts them with chorizo.</p>
      <p>Pairing sea and land is the signature of Les Coltineurs. Le Parisien featured the dish in its story on surf & turf cooking, and Marie Claire listed it among the house's indulgent dishes to share.</p>
      <p>Share it over an aperitif with a glass of Loire white, or as a starter before the veal sweetbreads.</p>
    </div>
